   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "square number",
     "triangular number",
     "visualise"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Some sequences can be drawn. Square numbers 1, 4, 9, 16 make square arrangements of dots. Triangular numbers 1, 3, 6, 10 make triangles.\nSequences are related. Adding two neighbouring triangular numbers gives a square number: 3 plus 6 is 9. The sum of the first few odd numbers is a square: 1 plus 3 plus 5 is 9.\nSeeing a picture of a pattern helps us explain why it works."
    }
